    "message": "Own social_network_v1 in Rust, with its rules, the state context and the social action\n\nThe row knows which records were written, so the check of a tick reads only those; this retires\nsocial_relationships_valid and the social use of RecordWatch. observe_event, the observed contacts\nof the social step, capture and validation of the state context, and the handler's social action\nthat goes through run in Rust. Python rules stay the comparison base and say every refusal. The\nsocial shadow ignores key order only in a run that reverses dicts.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>",
